            {"question":"A community introduces food labeling and tobacco taxation to reduce NCD risk. This strategy is BEST classified as:","options":["Health education","Policy and regulation","Routine screening","Medication adherence"],"answer":"Policy and regulation"},
            {"question":"Which statement is FALSE regarding non-modifiable risk factors?","options":["Age is a non-modifiable risk factor","Gender is a non-modifiable risk factor","Family history is a non-modifiable risk factor","Physical inactivity is a non-modifiable risk factor"],"answer":"Physical inactivity is a non-modifiable risk factor"},
            {"question":"A 70-year-old adult is planning an exercise program. Which approach is MOST appropriate according to the lecture?","options":["Avoid all physical activity","Follow adult recommendations with additional focus on balance and flexibility, adapted to functional ability","Perform only vigorous exercise","Limit activity to 60 minutes per week regardless of ability"],"answer":"Follow adult recommendations with additional focus on balance and flexibility, adapted to functional ability"},
            {"question":"A patient wants to modify his plate according to the Healthy Eating Plate. Which meal pattern is MOST appropriate?","options":["Half processed meat, one quarter refined grains, one quarter pastries","Half vegetables and fruits, one quarter whole grains, one quarter healthy proteins","Half sugary drinks, one quarter red meat, one quarter margarine","Half refined grains, one quarter processed meat, one quarter fried foods"],"answer":"Half vegetables and fruits, one quarter whole grains, one quarter healthy proteins"},
            {"question":"According to the MCQ section included in the lecture, which dietary pattern is MOST associated with cardiovascular protection?","options":["High-fat ketogenic diet","Mediterranean diet","Western fast-food diet","Low-protein diet"],"answer":"Mediterranean diet"},
