            {"question":"Mixed urinary incontinence is BEST described as:","options":["A combination of stress and urge incontinence","Urine leakage during sleep only","Temporary incontinence caused by medication","Incontinence caused by structural abnormalities only"],"answer":"A combination of stress and urge incontinence"},
            {"question":"A patient has repeated urine leakage because the bladder does not empty completely. Which type is MOST likely?","options":["Functional incontinence","Overflow incontinence","Stress incontinence","Bedwetting"],"answer":"Overflow incontinence"},
            {"question":"Which situation BEST represents functional urinary incontinence?","options":["Urine leakage when coughing","Strong urge despite an empty bladder","Recognition of the need to void but inability to reach the bathroom because of limited mobility","Leakage caused by an incompletely emptied bladder"],"answer":"Recognition of the need to void but inability to reach the bathroom because of limited mobility"},
            {"question":"Episodic urinary incontinence occurring while asleep is known as:","options":["Transient incontinence","Bedwetting","Structural incontinence","Overflow incontinence"],"answer":"Bedwetting"},
