            {"question":"An older adult avoids social activities because of embarrassment about urinary leakage. The nurse should recognize this as primarily:","options":["A psychological and social impact of urinary incontinence","A sign of improved continence","A normal and unavoidable effect of aging","A type of structural incontinence"],"answer":"A psychological and social impact of urinary incontinence"},
            {"question":"Which statement by the nurse is MOST appropriate when educating an older adult with urinary incontinence?","options":["“Urinary incontinence is a normal and unavoidable part of aging.”","“You should avoid telling anyone about your symptoms.”","“Urinary incontinence can be treatable and is not a normal part of aging.”","“You should permanently restrict all fluid intake.”"],"answer":"“Urinary incontinence can be treatable and is not a normal part of aging.”"},
            {"question":"Urinary incontinence is defined as any involuntary leakage of urine.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True"},
            {"question":"Urinary incontinence always occurs as an unavoidable consequence of aging.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False"},
