            {"question":"Which statement is correct regarding urinary incontinence and aging?","options":["Urinary incontinence is an inevitable result of aging and cannot be treated","Urinary incontinence is more common with aging but is treatable and not inevitable","Urinary incontinence always affects men more than women","Urinary incontinence has no relationship to medications"],"answer":"Urinary incontinence is more common with aging but is treatable and not inevitable"},
